Build option MESEN_ABSOLUTE_PADDLE: the Arkanoid controller's knob is where
the host says it is.

Mesen moves the knob by the mouse's movement since the last read, which
makes its position depend on every frame before. A tool-assisted run wants
the knob's position to be the frame's own input, as a movie holds it. With
this option the host sets the device's X coordinate to the position, from
0 to 160 (the knob's range, 0x54 to 0xF4, less 0x54), and the controller
reads it from there at each strobe.

--- a/Core/NES/Input/ArkanoidController.h
+++ b/Core/NES/Input/ArkanoidController.h
@@ -40,9 +40,16 @@
 
 	void RefreshStateBuffer() override
 	{
+#ifdef MESEN_ABSOLUTE_PADDLE
+		//A host that knows where the knob is (a movie's value for the frame)
+		//sets it as the X coordinate, from 0 to 160, instead of moving it:
+		//the knob's position is then the frame's input and nothing else.
+		int32_t newValue = 0x54 + GetCoordinates().X;
+#else
 		MouseMovement mov = GetMovement();
 
 		int32_t newValue = (int32_t)_currentValue + mov.dx;
+#endif
 		if(newValue < 0x54) {
 			newValue = 0x54;
 		} else if(newValue > 0xF4) {
